Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]` to return the first word. Since Python uses 0-based indexing, the first element of the list is at index 0, not 1. This caused:
- test_basic to fail: returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- test_single to error: tried to access index 1 when only index 0 existed

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
